<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  Wafer-handling cell — Gazebo Harmonic (gz-sim 8)
  ===========================================================================
  FRAME:  world z = 0 is the TOP SURFACE of the wooden workbench.
          +X = wafer flow, M1 Pro -> Pro 600.  +Z up.  Ground at z = -0.9906.

  MEASURED (owner, imperial -> metric):
      bench slab   60 x 24 x 1 in   = 1.5240 x 0.6096 x 0.0254 m
      top height   39 in            = 0.9906 m above ground
      legs         1.5 x 1.5 in     = 0.0381 m square, 0.9652 m tall
      leg inset    2 in from the long (60") edges, 8 in from the short (24")
      leg centres  x = +/-0.53975   y = +/-0.23495
      wafer        5 in diameter    = 0.1270 m  -> radius 0.06350

  EXACT geometry from customer STLs:
      wafer_tower  107.5 x 135.0 footprint, 100 tall, shelves at 50/72/94 mm
      belt_holder  180 (along belt) x 70 (across) x 45 tall, flat top

  CONVEYOR MESH — third-party, treat with suspicion:
      Sourced from a 3D Warehouse SketchUp model, converted to STL. It is in
      METRES (scale 1.0, not 0.001) and its facet winding was inconsistent
      (5518 of 11603 facets had inverted normals) — repaired in place.
      Overall 698 x 214.5 x 62.6 mm, belt carrying surface 36.0 mm above the
      model origin, i.e. z = 0.06265 with the frame sat on the bench.
      The 698 mm length agrees with the photo estimate, but NOTHING here is
      verified against the real DT-AC-CB070-02E. Used for VISUAL ONLY;
      collision is a primitive box. Metrology: belt_width_and_length,
      belt_top_height.

  LAYOUT — read off a plan-view photograph the owner sent IN CHAT on
  2026-09-03. THAT IMAGE IS NOT IN THIS REPO: there is no reference_photos_6
  directory, and an earlier version of this header wrongly cited one. The
  layout below therefore has NO artifact backing it. See PROJECT_CONTEXT.md
  section 14 - the owner has since confirmed this layout is WRONG.
      conveyor y = +0.130.  NOTE: the plan-view PHOTO read as "hard against
      the far edge" (+0.170); the reference RENDER the owner supplied on
      2026-09-03 clearly shows bench behind the belt, so it is now +0.130.
      Both are eyeballed - 40 mm apart. Metrology: belt_centreline_y.
      M1 Pro  far-LEFT corner   base (-0.560, +0.150)
      Pro 600 RIGHT edge        base (+0.620, +0.180)
      Both were moved FORWARD on 2026-09-03: at y +0.220 / +0.200 the M1 Pro's
      own base casting hung 30 mm off the rear edge and its plate 45 mm, and
      the Pro 600 plate had only 4.8 mm of margin. Caught by an AABB audit of
      every visual against the bench rectangle - an earlier check tested
      footprint CENTRES only, which all passed while the parts overhung.
      Re-run it with scripts/check_extents.py after moving anything.
      yellow tower  near-left   (-0.500, -0.120)
      blue tower    near-right  (+0.550, -0.120)
      BOTH towers carry the SAME pose, so both open the same way. Verified
      from the STL, not by eye: the material centroid sits 22 mm to -Y of the
      bbox centre, i.e. the C opens toward +Y - toward the arm that serves it.
      Confirmed again in the PLAN VIEW capture (docs/cell_plan.png).

      SHELVES ARE MEASURED off the mesh, not assumed. Upward-facing horizontal
      faces cluster at STL y = 0 / 50 / 72 / 94 / 95 mm; the three at 50/72/94
      each carry exactly 1760 mm2 of area (identical -> they are the nests),
      while 95 mm carries 1003 mm2 (the rim, not a shelf). With the model at
      z = 0.005 the nests are at world z = 0.0550 / 0.0770 / 0.0990.
      The wafer is spawned on the TOP nest, 0.0990 + half its 1.5 mm.

  ADDED 2026-09-03 from the owner's reference render:
      - black mounting plates under both arms (8 mm, OUTLINE + THICKNESS
        ASSUMED); both robots now stand at z = 0.008, not 0
      - M1 Pro blue fork (exact customer STL; MOUNTING assumed)
      - Pro 600 vacuum cup (primitives, not a scan; STEM LENGTH assumed)
      - both home poses re-solved by FK so the fork lies flat pointing -X and
        the cup points STRAIGHT DOWN; see generate_cell_urdf.py
      - light butcher-block top on dark legs, matching the render
      Reach checked: M1 Pro 314/345 mm to belt-A/yellow (400 mm reach);
      Pro 600 371/328 mm to belt-C/blue (600 mm reach). All on the bench.

  ⚠️  The SIDE and CORNER each unit occupies now come from the photograph, but
      the exact offsets and especially the BASE YAW angles are still unmeasured.
      Yaw is the highest-leverage number in the cell: 1 deg = ~7 mm at the
      M1 Pro's reach. Metrology: m1pro_base_yaw / pro600_base_yaw.
  ===========================================================================
-->
<sdf version="1.10">
  <world name="wafer_cell">

    <physics name="1ms" type="ignored">
      <max_step_size>0.001</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1.0</real_time_factor>
    </physics>

    <plugin filename="gz-sim-physics-system"           name="gz::sim::systems::Physics"/>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-user-commands-system"     name="gz::sim::systems::UserCommands"/>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-scene-broadcaster-system" name="gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster"/>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-contact-system"           name="gz::sim::systems::Contact"/>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-sensors-system"           name="gz::sim::systems::Sensors">
      <render_engine>ogre2</render_engine>
    </plugin>

    <gravity>0 0 -9.8066</gravity>

    <scene>
      <ambient>0.55 0.55 0.58 1</ambient>
      <background>0.78 0.82 0.87 1</background>
      <grid>false</grid>
    </scene>

    <light type="directional" name="sun">
      <cast_shadows>true</cast_shadows>
      <pose>0 0 6 0 0 0</pose>
      <diffuse>0.95 0.94 0.90 1</diffuse>
      <specular>0.25 0.25 0.25 1</specular>
      <direction>-0.35 0.4 -0.85</direction>
    </light>
    <light type="directional" name="fill">
      <cast_shadows>false</cast_shadows>
      <pose>0 0 4 0 0 0</pose>
      <diffuse>0.35 0.36 0.40 1</diffuse>
      <direction>0.5 -0.3 -0.75</direction>
    </light>

    <!-- ground plane + explicit 0.5 m reference grid drawn ON it. Gazebo's own
         <grid> would sit at world z=0, which here is the BENCH TOP, not the
         floor — misleading. This grid is at the real floor height. -->
    <model name="floor">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0 0 -0.99060 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="c"><geometry><plane><normal>0 0 1</normal><size>40 40</size></plane></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="v">
          <geometry><plane><normal>0 0 1</normal><size>40 40</size></plane></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.46 0.47 0.49 1</ambient><diffuse>0.58 0.59 0.61 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="floor_grid">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
      <visual name="gx1">
        <pose>-3.0 0 -0.9895999999999999 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.006 6.0 0.002</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.30 0.32 0.35 1</ambient><diffuse>0.38 0.41 0.45 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gy1">
        <pose>0 -3.0 -0.9895999999999999 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>6.0 0.006 0.002</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.30 0.32 0.35 1</ambient><diffuse>0.38 0.41 0.45 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gx2">
        <pose>-2.5 0 -0.9895999999999999 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.006 6.0 0.002</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.30 0.32 0.35 1</ambient><diffuse>0.38 0.41 0.45 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gy2">
        <pose>0 -2.5 -0.9895999999999999 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>6.0 0.006 0.002</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.30 0.32 0.35 1</ambient><diffuse>0.38 0.41 0.45 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gx3">
        <pose>-2.0 0 -0.9895999999999999 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.006 6.0 0.002</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.30 0.32 0.35 1</ambient><diffuse>0.38 0.41 0.45 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gy3">
        <pose>0 -2.0 -0.9895999999999999 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>6.0 0.006 0.002</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.30 0.32 0.35 1</ambient><diffuse>0.38 0.41 0.45 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gx4">
        <pose>-1.5 0 -0.9895999999999999 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.006 6.0 0.002</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.30 0.32 0.35 1</ambient><diffuse>0.38 0.41 0.45 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gy4">
        <pose>0 -1.5 -0.9895999999999999 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>6.0 0.006 0.002</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.30 0.32 0.35 1</ambient><diffuse>0.38 0.41 0.45 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gx5">
        <pose>-1.0 0 -0.9895999999999999 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.006 6.0 0.002</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.30 0.32 0.35 1</ambient><diffuse>0.38 0.41 0.45 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
